<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Cinderfall — the storm (owner's ruling, 2026-09-09: "Cinderfall
    storms"). Ash fall's rare, violent sibling: the same falling-particle
    trick, run at hard-snow density and tinted ember instead of grey, with
    real lightning underneath it.

    THE IGNITION IS VANILLA'S, NOT AN INVENTED ONE. `eventMakers` takes
    weather-event classes the base game already ships, and
    WeatherEvent_LightningStrike.DoStrike calls
    GenExplosion.DoExplosion(..., DamageDefOf.Flame, ...) at the strike
    cell (RimSage, RimWorld/WeatherEvent_LightningStrike.cs:44) — that IS
    the fire-starter, the same one DryThunderstorm uses. Nothing here
    invents an ignition system in XML; the intervals are simply tighter
    than DryThunderstorm's 1200 so the storm reads as a storm.

    That same strike is what this mod's existing fulgurite hook is
    postfixed onto (Source/FireEcologyHook.cs), so a cinderfall over sand
    leaves glass behind it as well as fire — no extra wiring, the hook was
    already listening for exactly this event.

    Ember tint, same mechanism as AshFall: Verse/SkyManager.cs:117 tints
    every non-forced overlay with `curSky.colors.overlay`, so the
    `<overlay>` colour below is what turns the hard-snow particle sheet
    into blown sparks and the fog layer into lit smoke.

    ⚠️ rainRate STAYS 0 here too — a storm that put out fires would be
    the opposite of the point, and RM_FE_BlackRain must remain the only
    rain-rated weather in the biome's table (see Pyrelands.xml).

    favorability VeryBad means WeatherDecider will not roll it in the
    first 8 days after settling (WeatherDecider.cs:156). That is correct
    for this one: it is the biome's disaster, not its wallpaper.
  -->

  <WeatherDef>
    <defName>RM_FE_Weather_Cinderfall</defName>
    <label>cinderfall</label>
    <description>A firestorm's exhaust arriving overhead: live embers driven sideways on a hot wind, thick enough to read by, coming down among the grass. Visibility collapses, the air is full of grit and sparks, and the lightning that comes with it lands in ground that is already primed to catch. Get everything flammable under a roof and get everyone off the grass.</description>
    <durationRange>12000~30000</durationRange>
    <favorability>VeryBad</favorability>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <perceivePriority>3</perceivePriority>
    <accuracyMultiplier>0.6</accuracyMultiplier>
    <moveSpeedMultiplier>0.85</moveSpeedMultiplier>
    <rainRate>0</rainRate>
    <snowRate>0</snowRate>
    <temperatureRange>0~999</temperatureRange>
    <windSpeedFactor>1.8</windSpeedFactor>
    <windSpeedOffset>1.5</windSpeedOffset>
    <preventSkygaze>true</preventSkygaze>
    <preventsShuttleLaunch>true</preventsShuttleLaunch>
    <letterDef>ThreatSmall</letterDef>
    <letterLabel>Cinderfall</letterLabel>
    <letterText>A cinderfall is coming down over the area. Live embers are falling among the grass and lightning is striking with them. Anything flammable left in the open is likely to catch, and anyone caught out in it will be burned.</letterText>
    <ambientSounds>
      <li>Ambient_Wind_Storm</li>
    </ambientSounds>
    <overlayClasses>
      <li>WeatherOverlay_SnowHard</li>
      <li>WeatherOverlay_Fog</li>
    </overlayClasses>
    <eventMakers>
      <li>
        <averageInterval>420</averageInterval>
        <eventClass>WeatherEvent_LightningFlash</eventClass>
      </li>
      <li>
        <averageInterval>640</averageInterval>
        <eventClass>WeatherEvent_LightningStrike</eventClass>
      </li>
    </eventMakers>
    <!-- `overlay` is the ember colour — see the header. -->
    <skyColorsDay>
      <sky>(0.72,0.44,0.28)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.90,0.86,0.84)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.95,0.46,0.16)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsDay>
    <skyColorsDusk>
      <sky>(0.70,0.36,0.22)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.90,0.86,0.84)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.92,0.42,0.14)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsDusk>
    <skyColorsNightEdge>
      <sky>(0.34,0.20,0.16)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.85,0.82,0.80)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.78,0.34,0.12)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightEdge>
    <skyColorsNightMid>
      <sky>(0.30,0.18,0.15)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.85,0.82,0.80)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.74,0.32,0.11)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightMid>
  </WeatherDef>

</Defs>
